@design/claude-mcp-server.sigil from ClaudeMcpServer import { cancel tool }
@design/delegation-service.sigil from DelegationService import {
  session cancel, stop notice,
}
@design/kernel.sigil from Kernel import { parent adapter, parent host }
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import { task id }

component ClaudePluginCommands {
  goal {
    Let a person who works in the Claude Code parent host stop their
    subzero tasks with a command they type that only the person can invoke.
  }

  state {
    ClaudePluginCommands is the parent adapter part of the plugin that gives
    the
    Claude Code parent host its commands, which are plugin skills that a person
    types. It runs no code of its own: each command asks Claude Code to call a
    tool of ClaudeMcpServer.

    The *cancel command* is the plugin skill /subzero:cancel. It takes an
    optional task id.
  }

  logic {
    On the cancel command with no task id, call the cancel tool with no
    task id,
    which runs a session cancel for the current parent session id and reports
    how
    many tasks were cancelled, which ends the flow.

    On the cancel command with a task id, call the cancel tool with that
    task id,
    which cancels that one task and reports it, which ends the flow.
  }

  constraints {
    The cancel command must be invoked only by the person, and the model must
    not be able to invoke it, because a cancel that the model chose could end
    work that the person wants.

    The cancel command must call the cancel tool and must not cancel a task by
    any other path, so that the stop notice and the session cancel are the ones
    of the cancel tool.

    The cancel command must pre-approve the cancel tool for its own invocation,
    so that a person who types it gets no approval prompt and needs no rule
    from the user or the project.
  }

  cases {
    With two running tasks of one parent session id, the cancel command with no
    task id ends both as cancelled and reports 2.

    With a running task, the cancel command with its task id ends that one task
    as cancelled and leaves the other tasks of the parent session id running.

    The model asks to invoke the cancel command and Claude Code refuses it,
    because only the person may invoke it.
  }

  interface {
    Offer the cancel command to a person in the Claude Code parent host, with
    an
    optional task id, so that it cancels the one task or every task of the
    current parent session id, and reports what it cancelled.
  }

  decisions {
    Escape does not stop a background task in the Claude Code parent host, so a
    person needs a command to stop all their subzero tasks. The command lives
    in its own component and not in ClaudeMcpServer because it is a plugin
    skill,
    and a later command of the plugin joins it here without growing the server.
  }
}
